            "review_title": "Review at Burger King",
            "review_text": "Leean W\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam206 contributions\n0\nWelcoming Staff at Burger King Thao Dien\nJan 2019 • Solo\nThe food at this branch is the same as all other branches, I particularly enjoy the chicken nuggets with french fries and the burgers but I am writing this review mainly to commend the wonderful attitude of the staff to people with disabilities. I often take out my friends 14 year old son to dine in various places. It is a little difficult for me as he has shaky walker as an aid and he has challenges walking and eating. But from the moment I am struggling to help him out of the taxi, the guard or member of staff rush out to help me carry him and always with warm welcoming smiles and greetings. My young friend has a lovely character so it's not difficult to warm to him but the staff at this branch of Burger King offer to help in the most natural, kind and warm way possible, My friend needs a little help with eating which is no problem to me at all but very often the staff will come across with extra tissues without being asked or come over and make some small talk. My young friend is Vietnamese and has some challenges talking, even though he is exceptionally intelligent, but the staff at the Thao Dien branch are patient and soon understand him perfectly. It is very significant that when I ask my friend's son where he would like to go with me for lunch, and I offer him various places for pizza, chicken or pasta etc. his answer is invariably 'Burger King D2' It is because these lovely people at the Thao Dien branch make my little friend so welcome and at ease that I am awarding a 5 star rating. They are staff to be proud of. Unfortunately I don't know their names but I guess that if they ever come across this review then hopefully they will know who they are. They are golden people.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 9, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
